Today we are going to recreate a project that I created on another machine. This project is called KT-Agent. KT stands for knowledge transfer and the agent portion should  
be clear. The kicker is that this project is going to be created entirely from modular skills, commands, and a CLAUDE.md file. Today we will make an MVP version of this     
project but we will be building with the mindset that this project will be expanded to become its own sharable application. The beauty of this project which I'd like to     
maintain is that it is light weight and easily sharable.                                                                                                                     

So here is the project. KT-Agent is a knowledge ingestion and sharing application where Users and document their "domain knowledge" (project docs, workflows, troubleshooting experiences, anything they want really), and consumers can interact with the 'kt-agent' to ask questions and converse with an agent who pulls information only from the created knowledge base.

There are two personas who will interact with this project, users and consumers.

Users are those who add to the knowledge base. There are a variety of ways in which we can grow the knowledge base. The two methods we will focus on for the MVP is by uploading files or from an agent lead interview. As a cosmetic feature, the program also maintains a persona.md file which contains an overview of the agents domain knowledge and can even record and replicate the user's communication style as it learns from interviews.

Consumers are those who interact with the KT-agent to discuss problems or try to learn from some of the knowledge stored in the knowledge base. This should be managed from an /agent file created in this repo which can be called on command. The agent should use metadata to pull relevant files from the knowledge base dynamically based on the scope of the questions.

