Agent:
kt-agent describes how the agent will interact with CONSUMERS and how to use the knowledge base to answer questions and the persona.md to gain tone

Commands:
ingest - ingests all files in inbox/ then creates markdown files based on the content and distributes those files into their appropriate place within the knowledge folder. This command has a lot of responsibility handling all types of files and recognizing ceratin tags from cleanse and interview. It may become more practical to break up this command to distribute responsibility. after files are processed and added to the knowledge base, they are moved to inbox/processed/. Interview tags encourage the command to call the persona skill to update communication style based on an interview. The ingest command can also receive files with an accompanying side car from the cleanse skill. The files should be paired together with the side car containing suggested changes from request.
interview - conducts an interview with a user either on a topic decided by the user or one you get from a question. Interviews should generally stay to one topic with focused questions to keep responses from being too long and to get good coverage on one topic. interviews should average 5-8 questions. Users can string interviews together if they want. Each topic should have its own annotated transcript which will be passed directly into the inboxfolder as a markdown file. this will have an interview tag.
cleanse - this command has 2 potential uses. It's either called after an ingest automatically to evaluate the new files entering the knowledge base to maintain a maximum threshhold of redundancy, uphold file organization, and evaluate metadata and its relevance to each file. If changes need to be made, they are passed back into the inbox folder with a sidecar file which describes the changes suggested by the cleanse command.

Skills:
persona - persona is a skill that can be implicitly called by other commands to evaluate a file that is being processed and update the persona.md file which documents general knowlege topics and communication style of the user. Maintaining an accurate catalog/overview of the knowledge contained in the knowledge base is more important than updating the personality details of the agent.

Knowledge - this is the base directory for the entire knowledge base. For now this will contain subdirectories which contain markdown files with metadata. This may later be replaced with a more sophisticated system
knowledge/projects - knowledge related to architecture, design and contect for specific systems or applications
knowledge/references - reference material, links, glossary terms, and quick lookups
knowledge/troubleshooting - descriptions of issues encountered and steps which lead to the solution
knowledge/workflows - daily and recurring operational procedures run by the user

CLAUDE.md - a descripton of the project and instructions for which files to load upon session start and how users will interact with the agent. also lists the skills available and important specs.

config.yaml - Details pertaining to the project and its file structure. (I'm not so sure this is actually essential to the project)

persona.md - an overview of who the user is, lists and descriptions of general areas of expertise and details about communication style. This can be modified by the user but should generally be completed dynamically as users interact with the project.

General Notes about the project:
All skills and commands should be modular and have independent responsibilities. They should reference eachother to accomplish more complex workflows. Keep the scope of commands and skills small. Split them up when their scope creeps beyond one task. This project should remain light weight and transportable into anyones existing projects. Do not allow  skills or commands to develop overlapping responsibilities. Prioritize meta data especially summaries for skills and knowlege files as they will be used for discovery.

