In my opinion, the real innovation in this project is a new way to ingest and document domain knowledge. No body likes writing docs for their code or spending lots of time writing out workflows they've developed for others to follow. This project offers a solution to that. When considering expansion and scale for this project, we will likely focus on this aspect of the project. That being said, the ingest and cleanse commands are crutial for creating a maintainable "database" of .md files. At least until I maybe move to a rag system (not part of mvp)

